    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch12-15: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.21";
    dc:description "The sentence explains the history of theoretical science rather than stating a variable a dataset records. Bibliographies can show where formulas are common, and the same record fits many other reasons a field stays with tractable problems. No outcome would clearly confirm or refute the stated cause.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: A test would score theoretical domains for behavioral simplicity and for success of closed-form prediction, then isolate computational reducibility as the cause. The claim fixes neither the scores nor a way to separate that cause from other histories of the same fields.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Fundamental reason is a historical cause that instrument limits, taste, and funding also fit.", "Little progress and not quite simple have no agreed measurement across sciences.";
